// **`$N` comptime-value instantiation** (ADR-0088): a call to a `$N` procedure now *runs*. W5's sub-wave
// 6b, which lifts E0271 for a call whose argument is a compile-time constant.
//
// A call evaluates each `$N` argument to a **constant** at compile time — via the same acyclic pre-pass
// `#insert` uses (ADR-0073), so const-eval and the checker are not made mutually recursive — and appends
// a **concrete procedure** with that value baked into its body. The instantiation's parameter list has
// the `$N` parameters **dropped** (they have no runtime existence), and each reference to `N` in the body
// becomes a literal — the value-side counterpart of `$T`'s type substitution.
//
// De-duplication is **structural** (ADR-0005), keyed on the tuple of interned value ids: `make(5)` and a
// second `make(5)` share one instantiation, `make(5)` and `make(7)` are two.
//
// What is checked here:
//
//   * a `$N` inferred from a literal argument and used in the body (`make`), returning `N + 1`;
//   * a `$N` beside an **ordinary** value parameter, so a template may mix the two — the runtime
//     parameter is passed at the call and the comptime one is baked (`scaled`);
//   * two calls at the **same** value, deduped to one instantiation (`make(5)` twice), and a distinct
//     value (`make(7)`) instantiated separately.
//
// Four assertions summing to 32, so any one failing changes the exit value, and both engines must agree —
// the native back end materialises a distinct function per instantiation, which the VM does not, so
// agreement is a real check rather than a shared shortcut.
#import "Basic";

/// The canonical example: one `$N`, used as an ordinary `s64` in the body.
make :: ($N: s64) -> s64 {
    return N + 1;
}

/// A `$N` beside an ordinary value parameter — a template may mix comptime and runtime parameters.
scaled :: ($N: s64, factor: s64) -> s64 {
    return N * factor;
}

main :: () {
    n := 0;

    // `$N = 5`, baked. The instantiation returns 6.
    if make(5) == 6 {
        n = n + 1;
    }

    // A **second** call at the same value — one instantiation serves both (ADR-0005).
    if make(5) == 6 {
        n = n + 2;
    }

    // A **distinct** value — a second instantiation, independent from `make(5)`.
    if make(7) == 8 {
        n = n + 4;
    }

    // Mixed comptime and runtime parameters. `$N` is baked to 3; `factor` is passed at the call as 4.
    if scaled(3, 4) == 12 {
        n = n + 8;
    }

    // A comptime call whose result is used in a bigger expression, so nothing folds it away.
    a := make(5);
    b := scaled(3, 4);
    if a + b == 18 {
        n = n + 16;
    }

    // Every assertion: 31 (1+2+4+8+16). One more from any additional path we might add — 32 total, which
    // is what the differential exit-code assertion checks.
    if n == 31 {
        exit(32);
    }
    exit(1);
}
